    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=-\\dfrac12(x-1)^3(x+2)$.",
      "worked": "The zeroes and their multiplicities give $P(x)=k(x-1)^3(x+2)$. Using $(2,-2)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=k(2-1)^3(2+2)\\\\-2&=4k\\\\k&=-\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $P(x)=-\\dfrac12(x-1)^3(x+2)$. Its leading coefficient is negative, so $P(x)\\to-\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty$, as required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
